# Third-party material shipped in this repository

## Cloud segmentation checkpoint

`src/uummannaq_ice/models/unet_mobv2_v2.pt`, 26,796,072 bytes.

**This is not our model.** The evidence is in the repository rather than in
memory. The legacy entry point this pipeline grew out of,
`archive/legacy_pipeline/ice-final/ice_classification_experimental_copy.py`,
declares `CHECKPOINT_FILE = "UNetMobV2_V2.pt"`, builds
`smp.Unet("mobilenet_v2", encoder_weights=None, in_channels=13, classes=4)` to
receive it, and loads it while stripping `module.` and `model.` prefixes with
`strict=False`. It contains no training code at all. Prefix stripping is what
you do to a checkpoint someone else saved, and the filename, the architecture
and the four-class CloudSEN12 label set all match the model published by the
CloudSEN12 project.

**What is not established, and what has to happen before this is redistributed
as anything.** The licence terms of that checkpoint are not recorded anywhere in
this repository, and they were not guessed here. Sitting in a public repository
is already redistribution, so the terms need to be read at the source, honoured,
and written into this file. If they turn out to forbid what this repository does
with them, there are three honest ways out: download the weights on first run
instead of shipping them, keep them in a separate artefact with their own terms,
or replace them with a permissively licensed cloud mask. The last one is the
worst of the three on the science, because
[docs/limitations.md](docs/limitations.md) shows every available alternative
either throws away the SWIR band that separates snow from cloud, or scores a
pixel against a history that a fjord does not have.

## Data

Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 imagery: Copernicus Sentinel data, processed by ESA.
Landsat 8 and 9 imagery: courtesy of the U.S. Geological Survey.
Sea ice index and concentration: National Snow and Ice Data Center.

Nothing in `archive/reprocessed_2026/` is raw imagery. Those files are counts and
statistics derived from it.
